>>
Rule 1 (image must be a 4D tensor; prevents ValueError and avoids get_shape-related issues)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 2 (all dimensions must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (height and width must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (channels dimension must be present)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 3) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 5 (image dtype must be floating-point)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 8 (numeric, orderable real values so finite differences are defined)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) * 0 = 0 ∧ min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 9 (shape access must be valid for all 4 dimensions; suppresses AttributeError: missing get_shape/shape)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, i) ∧ ndim(v_1) = 4
